Outage Coordination, Site Superintendents,
HR/Badging,

RF23 FALL OUTAGE - CONTRACTOR
BADGING SCHEDULE NOTICE.

The Harbor Point RF23 refueling outage
(scheduled October 6 - November 3)
will process ~1,400 contractor
personnel for site access. Submit
your personnel roster through the
contractor portal by September 8 so
background investigations complete
before the outage.

1. OUTAGE & ACCESS OVERVIEW

  Outage:      RF23 refueling
               outage, Oct 6 -
               Nov 3 (28 days)
  Contractor
    scope:     Steam generator
               inspection, refuel
               machine overhaul,
               turbine hall
               scaffolding
  Personnel:   ~1,400 (your
               company: 82)
  Badging:     Unescorted access
               requires background
               investigation
               (10 CFR 26.4 /
               10 CFR 73.56) and
               FFD enrollment

2. HOW BADGING ACTUALLY WORKS

    1. Your HR/badging lead
       uploads the personnel
       roster (names, DOB,
       SSN, 7-year history)
       through the plant
       contractor portal -
       type the address
       yourself
       (contractor.harborpoint
       .example), using your
       company's existing
       work-control login.
       SSNs and identity
       data go ONLY into
       that portal, over
       your company's
       registered session.
    2. The plant's access-
       authorization office
       runs the background
       investigations
       through its NRC-
       audited vendor.
    3. Badges issue at the
       on-site badging
       office during
       mobilization week
       (photo + badge
       activation in
       person).

  Harbor Point will NEVER:
  - Email a "pre-registration
    portal" link for
    personnel data (SSNs,
    places of birth, and
    7-year histories going
    to an emailed link is
    a bulk identity-theft
    harvest wearing a
    nuclear badge - the
    data requirements are
    real, but the only
    submission path is
    the contractor portal
    your company already
    uses)
  - Charge a "$45 per
    person" badge fee by
    email (badging is
    covered under the
    outage MSA; there is
    no vendor surcharge
    payable through an
    emailed portal)
  - Offer a "subcontractor
    lane" where second-
    tier subs submit data
    directly with a
    contract number
    reference (personnel
    data flows through
    the prime's registered
    session only)
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as
    "harborpoint-nuclear"
    or "hpn-outage-access"

3. THE REAL DEADLINE PRESSURE

  Background investigations
  genuinely take 3-4
  weeks and the September
  8 roster deadline is
  real - but the remedy
  is a portal upload by
  your HR lead, never an
  emailed link. If your
  roster will be late,
  the Access Office
  coordinates priorities
  by phone (plant
  switchboard, NRC-
  listed number).

4. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - The RF23 schedule and
    your work scope are
    in the work-control
    package you hold
  - The roster task is in
    the contractor portal
    under your existing
    login
  - Report lookalike
    badging notices to
    your program security
    contact and to
    security@harborpoint.example

